NEEDS TESTING
===========================================================================
- better handling of spec querying
	- libspecialization updates during m+ runs. need to figure out why
- [needs testing:] support tracking externals when it's unambiguous
    - three levels of ambiguity, maybe an option for behavior:
        1. (most important) is there only one person in the group that can cast the
           external? this is usually true unless multiple paladins
        2. is the external identifiable ON ALL GROUP MEMBERS? ironbark (12s duration)
           might be identifiable on most group members, but the resto druid who can
           cast ironbark also has barkskin (12s), which means the tracker will fail
           when the druid barks themselves.
        3. is the external distinguishable from OTHER EXTERNALS? ironbark and sac
           are a good example. both are 12s durations (though sac could be less),
           meaning a group with a prot pal and a resto druid could only 
           determine which was cast in two scenarios:
            a. the target was the prot paladin (then the spell was ironbark, sac
               can't be self-cast).
            b. the sac timed out early due to the 20% health tripwire AND the
               short duration doesn't match any other cds of the sac's target.
            (a) is actually common, so the tracker may still have some value. if the
            druid specs 16s ironbark, then it's likely fully identifiable


FEATURES
===========================================================================
- hide cooldown swipe on active static buffs
- ALL raidFlag and raidInCombatFlag values need to be checked! cannot dump them automatically
- cross-confidence layer consistency check
- maybe ADDON_LOADED is a better event for allocating stuff (not anchoring)
- add iconId for all database spells for static tracker
- for instant tracking: flag spells as static icons when they're identified
  by the 0-knowledge system and use that flag to decide where to send the cooldown
  icon.
- on death: at least clear active cooldown glows for all static icons
    - i guess a UNIT_AURA that removes all auras doesn't fire on death?
- inferAbility() - save the conflicting spells/casters for UI elements
- would be nice to firm up two object classes: Buff and HistoryItem, where Buff represents
  the aura itself and HistoryItem only handles tracking and display duties.
- option to disable all inference (@Aryella WoWUIDev)
- updating/clearing tracker data
    - when party members join/leave group or change positions
    - could be easier to just clear for now, but could be annoying if,
      e.g., you're looking at CDs when a key ends and a group member drops
      party and deletes all of your info.
    - update (likely clear, since there is a memory leak by design) between keys.
	    - is there a different event when changing zones vs. starting a mythic+ key?
    - add reset button to the /pdh solution window
- check tier bonuses to make sure they don't alter duration/charges/CDR/etc.
- get data to make better estimates on duration solve tolerance
    - both the "match" epsilon and the minimum difference
- how to handle sac in "solved" interface? (since its duration is _less than or
    equal to_ 12s, meaning it clashes with almost every defensive buff
    - solved interface should perhaps be the most conservative solution, meaning
      exact duration matches, no advanced inference (CD tracking, variable duration, etc)
    - turns out there's an external flag on sac, so this is less of a problem
    - need to figure out ironbark+sac in the same group
- maybe consider using aurasUpdated
    - turns out almost everything about fiery brand is bugged so can't work on this
    - can be useful for fiery brand, sentinel (due to buff stacks ticking down)
- support for detecting death?
    - UNIT_DIED exists, but surprisingly is secret. could we guess someone died
      if a ton of auras were removed in one batch and a UNIT_DIED fired sometime
      recently? PLAYER_TARGET_DIED fired in a follower dungeon when the NPC tank died
- better handle CDR
    - can compute upper bounds (or averages) on the amount of CDR gained. e.g., throwing
      avenger's shield on CD at 5 targets = 5s CDR per 12s (though procs reduce this
      and so does divine toll).:
- better handling/inference for abilities with charges
    - tanks are very charge heavy, so will be important
- updateRow
    - e.g., when specText or cpfMapping change, update the associated
      text widgets rather than forcing the functions that update those
      values to do it.
- talent informed database
    - requires extracting talent selections from talent string. apparently
      WA has code to do this.
- continue filling out spec ability database
- consider a different event than OnUpdate for cooldown timers since this
  fires every frame.
- options panel
    - text sizes
    - text outlines
    - font probably
    - direction
    - "omnicd mode" - moving the center debuff out of the frame
    - max history size
    - icon size
    - icon padding
    - add reset button to panel, have /pdh open options panel rather than reset
    - spell categories to track
        - important
        - big defensive
        - external
        - special (RAID_IN_COMBAT + at least one of the above, blessing of freedom
          might be the only one of these)



BUGS
===========================================================================
- DOESN'T WORK WHEN SOLO
    - libspec doesn't fire a second time, so static rows aren't populated
    - even requires /reload after joining a group
    - gives this error when it happens
        PetesDefensiveHistory.lua:194: attempt to index field 'items' (a nil value)
- handle shared cooldown between BoP and spellwarding
    - amusingly, which is cast can be differentiated 
- gift of the golden valkyr doesn't track if occurs during goak
    - because this is recorded as an update to the previous goak
- solution UI:
    - when an offline character is in group, somehow abilities get put into
      pdhGroupCDs that (a) don't make any sense (e.g., ardent defender in a
      druid+shaman group) and (b) before updatePdhGroupSolution() was ever
      run. results in ability != nil but ability.solved=nil and ability.conflicts=nil
    - maybe the offline player's nil specId causes a lua error in updatePdhGroupSolution
      that ends the function execution before getting to the identifyAbility() block?
    - [think solved] this isn't related to an offline member, it's when identifyAbility() dies due to a runtime error



LIMITATIONS
===========================================================================
- other players MUST be using some addon that has LibSpec embedded. The
  usual one is big/littlewigs (I guess). Could also say that everyone needs
  to run PetesDefensiveHistory.. :)
- defensives are identified by appearing in blizzard's center big buff
  frame. since blizzard shows only a single buff, rules were created to
  decide which buff to show if several are activated. e.g., for tanks with
  multiple def buffs (prot pal: ardent defender, goak) or when an external
  is applied to someone whose own buff is already running (e.g., applying
  ironbark to a hunter that already popped survival of the fittest).

  if two buffs are applied at the same instant, only one can appear as the
  icon, so one of the two will not be tracked.
    - i don't know what this logic is. most of the time it seems to show
      the latest applied buff.



TALENT CHECKING
===========================================================================
just some notes on using LibSpecialization to check specific talents

The series of functions below seems to be what produces the talent string:
- activeConfigID = C_ClassTalents_GetActiveConfigID()
- talentString = C_Traits_GenerateImportString(activeConfigID)

example code on how to traverse the talent tree
https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dragonflight_Talent_System


some code about the serialization process
https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/live/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_PlayerSpells/ClassTalents/Blizzard_ClassTalentImportExport.lua


just libspec on github. looks like the addon uses chat messages to
communicate with group members. perhaps it sends them the code as a
string and asks them to run it? seems insecure.
https://github.com/BigWigsMods/LibSpecialization/blob/master/LibSpecialization/LibSpecialization.lua


weakauras had a decoder library:
https://github.com/WeakAuras/WeakAuras2/blob/cabde3e6c9419516889cd0305b358c749f90f2ca/WeakAuras/LibSpecializationWrapper.lua#L154




DONE
===========================================================================
- the blessing of freedom problem: it's an external castable on anyone but it isn't flagged
  as external, so any group with a paladin puts an 8s duration (1,0,0) flagged ability
  on everyone. turns out it's HELPFUL|RAID flagged and that allows major disambiguation
- stop using blizzard's CenterDefensiveBuff (just hide it) so that multiple active buffs and
  non-defensive buffs can be supported
- add spell caster inference with UNIT_SPELLCAST_SUCCEEDED
    - HALF 1: track casts
    - HALF 2: use the info
- handle instant inference in the cases where it's possible
    * for buffs that are unique without duration info
    * align these buffs next to frames omniCD style
    * these never enter the history tray
- add instant tracking
- better inference using cooldown tracking
    - e.g.: prot paladin has AD=8s and GoAK=8s so they can't be distinguished.
      if AD and GoAK are used in sequence, we don't know which was used first, but
      the only way to have 2 8s buffs is if they were both used. so now can infer
      AD is on cd and one charge of GoAK is used. so if we see another 8s buff on
      the paladin, we know it was charge 2 of GoAK and now both charges are on CD
      for some time. AD will probably come off CD during this period, meaning that
      the next CD is likely AD.
        - gets a little murkier since GoAK is also a CDR spell
- separate the bookkeeping of updatePdhGroupSolution() from the inference logic
- make a unified inference function. it should be able to work on empty cooldown
  tracking/cast tracking/etc. tables to simulate a "no-knowledge" state for the
  solutions UI
- addon namespace global cleanup
- use blizzard's filters for more info (HELPFUL|BIG_DEFENSIVE, HELPFUL|EXTERNAL, HELPFUL|IMPORTANT)
- now tracks frame sorting, properly mapping, e.g., player -> CompactPartyFrameMemberX
- don't place buff into the history until it finishes
	- possible with aura instance ID tracking
	- possible to handle the overlapping defensives where the buff icon
	  is changed before the last defensive completes
- track durations by UNIT_AURA removed list and auraInstanceID
- as new features have been added, updating the current data structures is
  too cumbersome to handle newer features.
	- new add/remove functions for history
	- new swap/clear/etc functions to fully abstract internal data architecture
	- better facilitate setup/teardown/update/reset
	- clarify data hierachy. individual cooldown frames need to know, e.g.,
	  to what player they refer. EITHER:
		1. copy all of this data into each frame and abstract away the cumbersome
		   duplication
		2. figure out how to link to a globally visible data structure.
		   this is cleaner, but depends on how wow scopes callback execution
- better guessing for:
    - duration_variable (should record whether this is < or > the stated duration)
        - in some cases fully unambiguous solutions remain. e.g.: DK AMS (<=7s) and
          IBF (=8s). if these are the only available spells for the group, then any
          duration <= 7s is definitely AMS and any 8s duration is definitely IBF.
        - in others, it becomes a best match. e.g.: paladin sac (<=12s) and just
          about every defensive. since the sac *CAN* end before 12s if the paladin
          drops below 20%, there's a chance it happens to wear off at exactly the
          duration of another defensive causing a misidentification. since the
          likelihood of this is low, the timer is still almost always useful.
            - because of these cases, it could be useful to keep an internal table
              of last-use of cooldowns. if an unambiguous sac happened (e.g.,
              a DK in a group with just a prot paladin and no other externals had
              a defensive that lasted 12s, then it was a sac) then we now know sac
              is unavailable for 60s, meaning that ambiguities caused by sac can
              be ignored for that 60s window.
- support tracking externals when it's unambiguous
    - until this support is implemented, should hide externals when they can be
      identified as it clutters the real cooldowns.
    - requires redirecting the icon from the target's party frame to
      the (inferred) caster's history.
- solving group inferences based on the full catalog of possible defensives
	- will be different per player. e.g., resto druids with 12s bark and
	  12s ironbark will never be solvable but every other group member
	  could be.
	- solution pane showing the current group members, each of their
	  possible cooldowns and which ones are identifiable
- infer ability based on duration
	- prune duplicate abilities in history when possible
- for unidentified abilities: remove the tracker text once the longest
  possible cooldown time for that player has been reached (i.e., max CD
  across all externals in the group and that player's own cds).
- handle when libspec never returns a spec
    - [UPDATE]: just requires all players have an addon (pref this one) with
      LibSpec embedded
- auras possibly being assigned to the wrong anchor?
	- case where arcane mage had blur in history?
    - [PROBABLY FIXED] older code assumed auraInstanceIDs were unique across
      characters when they might not be.
- use different textures when it makes sense (e.g., gift of the golden valkyr)
